course: dictionary
lesson: 10990
title: Warship: a ship for war
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A warship is a ship built for war. Break the word into its two parts, war and ship, and the meaning is already there: a ship that is used in a fight. Context helps you check this.
explain: «Greeks sailed in triremes, fast warships with three rows of oars, and traded olive oil, wine and pottery.» The words after the comma explain what a trireme is: a fast ship with oars. Then the word warship tells you it was built for fighting, and the Greeks also used it to trade.
explain: «The Portuguese did not simply join this trade: they used warships and forts to force others to buy passes and pay duties.» Here warships are used to make other people obey. A navy, which is the country's sea force, runs warships. If you swap in "fighting ship" and the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: A warship is a ship built and armed for fighting in a war, run by a navy.
fact: Warships include battleships, aircraft carriers, destroyers, frigates and submarines.
fact: «Warships» means ships built and armed for fighting, so the word is made from war and ship.
fact: «Triremes» were fast warships with three rows of oars.
fact: Warships can also be used to patrol seas and guard ships, as well as to fight.
exercise: «Greeks sailed in triremes, fast warships with three rows of oars, and traded olive oil, wine and pottery.» What is a warship? | A small fishing boat with a crew of two | *A ship built and armed for fighting in a war | A ship that carries people across a lake | A ship for carrying olive oil and wine
exercise: «The Portuguese did not simply join this trade: they used warships and forts to force others to buy passes and pay duties.» Find and copy one word that means ships built for fighting. | forts | trade | *warships | duties
exercise: Which of these is a warship? | A fishing trawler | *A destroyer | A ferry carrying cars across the sea | A rowing boat on a lake
test: «The Snake called the Crocodile a "self-propelling man-of-war" (a warship with armour on top).» What is a man-of-war here? | A type of rock | A sailor's knot | *A warship | A kind of fish
test: The word warship is made from two smaller words. Which two? | warm and ship | water and ship | *war and ship | wear and shop
exam: Which of these is NOT a type of warship? | A frigate | A submarine | An aircraft carrier | *A cruise liner carrying holiday makers
